# Harness integration

The bundle is generated in the KB with `integrate --generate`, reviewed, then installed
in the host with `integrate --apply`. Skill protocol {{skill_protocol}} uses one full
`SKILL.md` at `{{agents_skill_path}}`. Every harness gets a native instruction target
pointing to the same workflow; it need not discover that directory automatically.

| Harness | Instruction target |
|---|---|
| Codex | `AGENTS.md`; an existing `AGENTS.override.md` gets a pointer |
| Claude Code | `CLAUDE.md`; mixed installations retain `/kb` through a short command alias |
| Cursor | `.cursor/rules/kb.mdc`, with `alwaysApply: true` |
| Grok Build | `AGENTS.md` |
| GitHub Copilot | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` |
| Junie | `AGENTS.md`; an existing `.junie/AGENTS.md` gets a pointer |

The primary file is `{{core_source}}`. Other targets contain a short reference instead
of another full workflow or core. Exactly one physical skill directory is selected:
`.agents/skills/kb` when Codex or Cursor is enabled, otherwise `.claude/skills/kb`
for Claude, `.grok/skills/kb` for Grok, or `.kbw/skills/kb` for instruction-only
targets. Claude's mixed-installation command alias is `.claude/commands/kb.md`; it
forwards to the canonical workflow and preserves the existing slash command.

## Installation and recovery

Managed Markdown blocks preserve all surrounding user content. Standalone generated files
and the lock at `.kbw/integration.lock` carry exact hashes. An edited managed file or
block is a conflict. Obsolete managed copies are removed only if their locked content
still matches; modified copies remain conflicts. No symlink is followed for a write.

kb caps a generated skill at 16 KiB, a Copilot instruction file at 4000 bytes, a Cursor
rule at 8000 bytes and other managed instruction files at 16 KiB. These conservative kb
budgets do not represent a vendor's total prompt allowance. Always-on core is capped at
600 estimated tokens; overflowing rules, conditions and exceptions are never truncated.
Shorten the core or leave records scoped.

Generate and install again after knowledge or workflow changes. A core receipt is checked
against the selected snapshot, the bundle, the host lock, the actual instruction bytes
and the mounted launcher path. Read the source before passing it to context. Historical
replay must use frozen instructions and full context, not a current core.

## Load probes

`{{kb_path}}/kbw integrate --probe` checks the installed files and emits a challenge.
It explicitly leaves runtime loading unverified. Run the challenge in a fresh, trusted
session of each enabled harness; preserve the exact harness version, response and tool
calls. The marker must be reported before tools and the initial diagnose call must occur.
Do not include the expected marker in the challenge prompt. After updates, repeat this
probe before treating delivery as verified. Installation tests alone do not establish
model consultation, compliance or task quality.

For nested workspaces, inspect overriding instructions and the actual launch directory.
Personal/global skills, user settings, trust decisions and vendor loading limits remain
outside the generated bundle. The probe must reflect the real host configuration.

## Official loading contracts

Checked 2026-10-06. Recheck when upgrading a harness.

- [Codex AGENTS.md](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/agents-md)
  describes override precedence and the instruction byte limit.
  [Codex customization](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/overview#skills)
  describes repository skills in `.agents/skills`.
- [Claude skills](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills) documents
  `.claude/skills` and the backward-compatible `.claude/commands` format.
- [Cursor rules](https://cursor.com/docs/rules) documents `.mdc` and `alwaysApply`;
  [Cursor skills](https://cursor.com/docs/skills) documents compatibility skill roots.
- [Grok skills and compatibility](https://docs.x.ai/build/features/skills-plugins-marketplaces)
  documents `.grok/skills`, Claude compatibility and `AGENTS.md`.
- [Copilot instructions](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/customize-copilot/add-custom-instructions)
  documents repository instructions and the session's `/instructions` view.
- [Junie guidelines](https://junie.jetbrains.com/docs/guidelines-and-memory.html)
  documents `.junie/AGENTS.md` taking precedence over root guidance.
